#WRITE(PTR, $000001E2)
I was completely winded. My lungs struggled to shovel air in and%Nout, and my agonized panting echoed throughout my room.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000001F2)
I plopped down in my computer chair.
<LINE>
My body and clothes were completely drenched in sweat.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000202)
What the *fuck* had just happened?
<LINE>
Another one of my delusions?
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000212)
My nausea was becoming unbearable. Trying to alleviate it,%NI grabbed a Cola from the fridge and chugged it as fast as I could.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000222)
That delusion was way too realistic—even for my usual%Nstandards—and boy, was it gruesome. Too gruesome.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000232)
I was *still* out of breath.%NCould a simple delusion really do this to me?
<LINE>
...No, it definitely couldn’t.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000242)
I felt an uncomfortable sensation in my right hand.
<LINE>
I’d been clenching my fist so hard, my fingers had nearly turned %Nwhite.
<LINE>
I hadn’t even noticed until just now.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000252)
I slowly opened my hand, one finger at a time, all while my heart%Npounded like a drum.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000002B8)
【拓巳】
“Eek...!”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000002C8)
Lying in the palm of my hand... was a single stake.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000392)
Terrified by the sight of it, I instinctively turned and threw it%Nagainst the wall.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000404)
That was the stake from before...!
<LINE>
Well, I definitely *did* pick one up off the ground earlier, but...
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000414)
How was that even possible?
<LINE>
Hadn’t it all been just a delusion?!
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000424)
I don’t know, I don’t know, I don’t know!%NIt can’t be possible!
<LINE>
It can’t be, it can’t be, it can’t be!
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000004D0)
At my wits’ end, I started pacing around my room. I needed to figure out whether that nightmare had been real, or just another%Ndelusion.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000534)
That was the plan, at least, until I slipped on a CD case and lost%Nmy balance. In a panic, I reached out for something to keep myself%Nfrom falling flat on the floor.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000544)
I barely managed to find something to latch on to, but%Nunfortunately, that “something” was my shelf of waifus.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000005AA)
Before I had the chance to regret it, it was already too late.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000005BA)
In the end, no matter how hard I tried, I wasn’t able to stop myself from falling ass-first onto the floor.%NAnd to make matters worse, several of my beautifully arranged%Nfigures came tumbling down on top of me.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000005CA)
Ugh... Goddammit...
<LINE>
This was the worst. Everything about this was just the worst...
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000624)
I let out a groan as I rose to my feet. I had to make sure my%Nfigures were safe.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000067E)
【拓巳】
“Aauugh! Ignis-tan from Jingai Makyo! Your swooord...!”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000068E)
It’d snapped clean in two.
<LINE>
Why did it have to be one of the expensive ones? I’d paid a%Npremium online for this!
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000006AE)
【拓巳】
“God damn it! You’ve gotta be fucking kidding me!”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000006BE)
I tried putting the two halves of the blade back together, but I’d%Nnever be able to fix it perfectly, even if I used glue. Any value%Nit’d once had was now gone.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000006CE)
【拓巳】
“Gimme a fucking break! Fuck, fuck, fuck, fuck, FUCK!”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000006EA)
I turned to my chair and kicked it out of sheer rage.
<LINE>
Tears began to well up in my eyes.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000006FA)
Why did I have to go through all this? What had I ever done to%Ndeserve this?!
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000070A)
I fell to the floor and just sat there for a while, heartbroken,%Nstaring dejectedly at my now-swordless Ignis-tan.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000782)
【拓巳】
“...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000792)
Once the storm of anger and confusion had passed,
<LINE>
I found my mind filling with visions of “her” face, along with%Nthat “modern art” I’d seen.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000007A2)
I had actually been physically holding one of those stakes.
<LINE>
Which meant it couldn’t’ve been a delusion. It had all been real.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000007B2)
I really wanted to deny it, but there was no way I could.
<LINE>
By tomorrow, it was sure to be all over the media.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000007C2)
I really, *really* didn’t want anything to do with this nightmare.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000007D2)
There was no way associating with that “girl”—no, that%N*demon*—could bring anything but catastrophe for me.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000007E2)
Hell, we’d only just met for the first time, and there had already%Nbeen a disaster.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000007F2)
After all, I’d brought home a critical piece of evidence from that%Nincident: one of the stakes that’d been used in the murder.
<LINE>
I wouldn’t be surprised if that on its own was enough to make me%Na suspect.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000802)
And... And if things weren’t already bad enough, that demon had%Nseen my face...
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000812)
There was no way out of this mess...
<LINE>
At this rate, I was going to... that demon was going to...
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000822)
No, forget about that. For now, I should focus on getting things%Nsorted in my head. For my own sake.
<LINE>
If I valued my own life, I really needed to figure things out...
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000093E)
【拓巳】
“No doubt about it.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000094E)
【拓巳】
“That picture must have been some sort of advance notice for the%Nmurder.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000095E)
Otherwise, there’d be no way the image could have matched up so%Nperfectly with the crime scene.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000096E)
First she’d edited that image together, then she’d recreated it in%Nreal life, right down to the finest detail.%NThat was how the crime had happened. ...No, in her eyes, I bet it%Nwas more of a “work of art” than a “crime.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000097E)
She seemed like that kind of psycho—dedicated to finishing any%Njob with nothing but sheer perfection.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000098E)
【拓巳】
“She’s fucked up in the head...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000099E)
【拓巳】
“But why show that picture to *me*...? And wait, how did she know%NI was Neidhardt? And how the hell did she know my real name?!”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000009AE)
Uuugh... What was I supposed to do...?
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000009BE)
That demon would definitely come to kill me soon.
<LINE>
If she already knew my name, e-mail, and all that stuff, then there was a very good chance she knew my home address too.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000009CE)
I curled up into the fetal position in my chair.
<LINE>
The image of that twisted murder was etched into my mind. How could I stay calm when I could end up that way too?
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000009DE)
【拓巳】
“I don't wanna die! I don't wanna die! I don't wanna die!%NI don't wanna die! I don't wanna die! I don't wanna die―”%K%P
